<section id="1001I_S000I" variety="S000I">
<name>Door Lock</name>
<ttl id="1001I_S000I_744CR_T004N" variety="T004N">
<name>Wireless Door Lock Control System</name>
<para id="RM0000005BA00RX" category="J" type-id="300MC" name-id="622PC-00" from="200612">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>No Answer-back (Hazard + Buzzer)</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM0000005BA00RX_02" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00002C700000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>If there is no answer-back even though the wireless door lock and unlock operate, a malfunction in the hazard output from the instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU) and the wireless buzzer output from the smart key computer assembly (certification ECU) is suspected.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>The wireless door lock control system has functions that use multiplex communication. First, follow "How to Proceed with Troubleshooting" and confirm that there is no malfunction in the communication system before proceeding with troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When using TaSCAN with the ignition switch OFF, repeatedly turn any door courtesy light switch ON←→OFF until communication between TaSCAN and the vehicle starts. (ON←→OFF interval within 1.5 seconds)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When the electrical key transmitter or smart key computer assembly (certification ECU) has been replaced, refer to the registration procedure in the immobiliser reference section.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Confirm that DTC B1242 is not output before proceeding with troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Check that there are no other electrical key transmitters in the vehicle interior.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000005BA00RX_03" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00002C800000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B167605J01" width="7.106578999in" height="5.787629434in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000005BA00RX_04" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000005BA00RX_01" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM0000005BA00RX_01_0019" proc-id="RM0550J___00005H700000">
<testtitle>Check Customize Settings</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), check that the customize data "Operation Confirmation Buzzer (Answer-back Buzzer)" is set to "ON".</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Set to "ON"</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000005BA00RX_01_0001" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000005BA00RX_01_0022" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000005BA00RX_01_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___00002C000000">
<testtitle>Check Wireless Door Lock Operation</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Check whether lock/unlock operates by wireless operation.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>If the wireless door lock and unlock operate, it can be confirmed that the wireless command from the transmitter is being input to the certification ECU and main body ECU.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000005BA00RX_01_0015" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000005BA00RX_01_0008" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000005BA00RX_01_0015" proc-id="RM0550J___00002C500000">
<testtitle>Inspect Answer-back</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Check which answer-back function does not operate.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt/>
</specitem>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.54in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.59in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Hazard warning lights do not operate</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Buzzer does not operate</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000005BA00RX_01_0002" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="RM0000005BA00RX_01_0020" fin="false">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000005BA00RX_01_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___00002C100000">
<testtitle>Check Hazard Warning Light Output</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Check that the turn signal lights blink when the hazard switch is pressed.</ptxt>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000005BA00RX_01_0004" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000005BA00RX_01_0009" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
